@*
    Library assistant, floating.

    Three things changed here.

    The robot mark appeared three times at once when the panel opened: on the launcher, in the
    panel header, and again as a large decorative stage with orbiting dots. Exactly one is shown
    now — the launcher carries the mark while closed and becomes a close button while open, so the
    header mark is the only one on screen once the panel is up. The decorative stage is gone; it
    was pure ornament between the header and the first message.

    The mark itself was a blue SVG with baked-in #193d87/#2e86c4 fills, which is why the assistant
    read as a foreign widget pasted onto an orange-and-charcoal site. It is a themed glyph now and
    inherits the palette like everything else.

    The quick actions all send real questions to /assistant/ask. They used to include two that
    served hard-coded text instead; see chatbot.js for why that mattered.
*@

<div id="homeChatbot" class="home-chatbot" aria-live="polite">
    <button type="button" id="homeChatbotToggle" class="home-chatbot__toggle" aria-expanded="false"
            aria-controls="homeChatbotPanel" aria-label="Library assistant">
        @* Both glyphs ship; CSS shows whichever matches the open state, so the launcher is the
           mark when closed and the dismiss control when open. *@
        <i class="bi bi-stars home-chatbot__toggle-icon home-chatbot__toggle-icon--open" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <i class="bi bi-x-lg home-chatbot__toggle-icon home-chatbot__toggle-icon--close" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    </button>

    <section id="homeChatbotPanel" class="home-chatbot__panel" aria-label="Library assistant" hidden>
        <header class="home-chatbot__header">
            <span class="home-chatbot__avatar" aria-hidden="true">
                <i class="bi bi-stars"></i>
            </span>
            <div class="home-chatbot__heading">
                <h2 class="home-chatbot__title">Library assistant</h2>
                <p class="home-chatbot__status" id="homeChatbotStatus">Answers from the live catalogue</p>
            </div>
            <button type="button" id="homeChatbotClose" class="home-chatbot__close" aria-label="Close assistant">
                <i class="bi bi-x-lg" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </button>
        </header>

        <div id="homeChatbotMessages" class="home-chatbot__messages"></div>

        <div class="home-chatbot__quick-actions" id="homeChatbotQuickActions">
            @* Every one of these is a real question put to the live assistant. *@
            <button type="button" data-ask="What books do I have?">My books</button>
            <button type="button" data-ask="Do I owe any fines?">My fines</button>
            <button type="button" data-ask="What are my reservations?">My reservations</button>
            <button type="button" data-ask="How many books can I borrow?">Borrow limit</button>
            <button type="button" data-ask="What happens if I return a book late?">Late returns</button>
            <button type="button" data-ask="What are the opening hours?">Opening hours</button>
        </div>

        <form id="homeChatbotForm" class="home-chatbot__input-row">
            <label class="sma-sr-only" for="homeChatbotInput">Ask the library assistant</label>
            <input id="homeChatbotInput" type="text" maxlength="140"
                   placeholder="Where is Clean Code? Do I owe fines?"
                   autocomplete="off" />
            <button type="submit" aria-label="Send message">
                <i class="bi bi-send-fill" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </button>
        </form>
    </section>
</div>
